So far, I have played 42 tourists on NAO. This includes the whole
NetHack beginner phase. Ascended 13, i.e. 30%. Since I "try harder"
(wrath of Mog incident in January), I've played 9 tourists. Ascended
7, i.e. 77%. One was shot in the back with lightning in a dark mines
level above Minetown, the other died stupidly in a bones level to an
arch-lich below Minetown (had aweful lag, eventually moved off the <,
DYWYPI?). Tourists aren't as difficult as everyone makes them.

Tourists (and other humans relying on ranged combat (Ran/Rog)) lack
infravision. You simply don't see monsters approaching in corridors or
dark areas like you do with other races. That's the whole problem. You
need to adjust your playing style to that. (If you don't believe this,
start a tourist in wizard mode, wish for a magic lamp and turn it on.
Survival becomes *considerably* easier.)

Don't melee with your darts. Put down Elbereth and throw them at the
fleeing monster when it's out of melee range. Avoid dark areas as much
as possible unless you have a light source, ESP or warning. Note that
tourists/rogues/rangers cannot start with a light source (the sneaky
DevTeam knows this would make it so much easier!). Use lit areas to
travel as much as possible. Throw a dart or some junk item along a
corridor to get a notice if a monster is lurking there (keep your pet
behind you). Since a light source is "win", Minetown is more important
than Sokoban for tourists. Enter the mines and stay on the upstairs.
Elbereth, Elbereth, Elbereth. Let your pet kill most of the monsters.
Throw darts at monsters. Put down more Elbereths. Wait until the scene
has quieted down and sort through the loot (armor, weapons). Then make
for the > (starting scrolls of magic mapping help here nicely). Repeat
until you reach Minetown. Now hope Izchak or someone else sells a lamp
or two. If you luck out and find a magic lamp (or generally get a
wish), wish for Magicbane. It will help you survive better than
anything else you can get at this point (MR, Elbereth, decent primary
weapon). Also consider that tourists can get basic in nearly every
weapon out there, so "wasting" a skill slot on scimitar, trident or
whatever decent weapon you might find early on will help you survive
as well. Oh, and use your camera. My last tourist survived a hilarious
Minetown situation because of it.

